rget across all authorities, then performs only the listed\n5413|per-target atomic renames. The Materialization Journal is the coordinator. A\n5414|crash may expose a prefix of committed authorities, but recovery MUST either\n5415|validate and finish that exact plan or restore all predecessors; it MUST never\n5416|call the prefix a successful materialization or publish a marker early.\n5417|\n5418|On Windows, open handles can prevent rename. The implementation MUST stop known\n5419|processes, retry boundedly, and fail with retained staging if atomic replacement\n5420|cannot be proven. It MUST NOT fall back to in-place partial overwrite.\n5421|\n5422|### 11.7 Conflict handling\n5423|\n5424|Workspace replication is enabled by default. Before materialization, the\n5425|destination is classified:\n5426|\n5427|- &lt;code>absent&lt;/code>;\n5428|- &lt;code>empty&lt;/code>;\n5429|- &lt;code>managed_unchanged&lt;/code>, matching its last checkpoint;\n5430|- &lt;code>managed_divergent&lt;/code>; or\n5431|- &lt;code>unmanaged_nonempty&lt;/code>.\n5432|\n5433|This ordered five-value registry is the canonical\n5434|&lt;code>DestinationClass&lt;/code> used by domain logic, RPC, CLI Result, journal\n5435|recovery, and Observation Events. The former spellings\n5436|&lt;code>matching_managed&lt;/code>, &lt;code>divergent_managed&lt;/code>, and\n5437|&lt;code>unmanaged&lt;/code> are invalid in version 1.0.0; &lt;code>empty&lt;/code> is never\n5438|collapsed into &lt;code>absent&lt;/code>.\n5439|\n5440|Only the first three MAY be committed automatically.\n5441|&lt;code>managed_divergent&lt;/code> and &lt;code>unmanaged_nonempty&lt;/code> MUST fail\n5442|closed with a structured comparison. The operator MAY then:\n5443|\n5444|- inspect &lt;code>ax diff&lt;/code>;\n5445|- materialize to a new copy;\n5446|- create a separate Git worktree;\n5447|- or explicitly replace a managed replica using\n5448|  &lt;code>--replace-managed-replica --expect-checkpoint CHECKPOINT_ID&lt;/code>.\n5449|\n5450|An unmanaged nonempty path MUST never be replaced. Before explicit managed\n5451|replacement, &lt;code>ax&lt;/code> MUST checkpoint and preserve the destination's\n5452|divergent state. Classification MUST use the Section 10.6 current marker and a\n5453|fresh content capture; SQLite or a directory-name convention is insufficient.\n5454|The current owner then emits\n5455|&lt;code>replica.replace_confirmed&lt;/code>: its expected checkpoint is the exact\n5456|checkpoint stored by the current marker, its expected marker ID is that exact\n5457|current marker, and its replacement checkpoint is the selected source\n5458|checkpoint. It next issues the matching &lt;code>managed_replica&lt;/code> Tombstone\n5459|with the confirmation event as its causal basis and emits\n5460|&lt;code>tombstone.issued&lt;/code>. The replacement Materialization Plan uses that\n5461|Tombstone ID and marker predecessor; without this event/Tombstone chain it MUST\n5462|fail before mutation.\n5463|Silent overwrite, timestamp-based overwrite, and broad path deletion are\n5464|forbidden.\n5465|\n5466|## 12. Workspace replication\n5467|\n5468|### 12.1 Workspace snapshot\n5469|\n5470|Every checkpoint references a workspace-group Transfer Manifest. The snapshot\n5471|MUST be &lt;code>kind = workspace_group&lt;/code> and carry the exact Section 10.4\n5472|&lt;code>WorkspaceSnapshot&lt;/cod\n… [25940 chars truncated for the reminder observer — judge from the claim and evidence of a check, not the full body]</tool-result>\n  </message>\n  <message role=\"assistant\">\n    <tool-call call-id=\"c18\" name=\"read_file\"><arguments>{\"path\":\"SPEC.md\",\"offset\":5890,\"limit\":600}</arguments></tool-call>\n  </message>\n  <message role=\"tool\">\n    <tool-result call-id=\"c18\">Read text file `SPEC.md`.\n(5889 line(s) above)\n5890|\n5891|1. Destination allocates one group operation ID and one session operation ID\n5892|   for each migration-cohort member. It calls &lt;code>handoff.prepare&lt;/code> for\n5893|   each, naming the identical WorkspaceGroupExpectation, source lease,\n5894|   destination host, expected source checkpoint, and MaterializationCohort whose\n5895|   two arrays both equal the selected migration cohort. A single-member cohort\n5896|   still carries the exact expectation and one-element arrays.\n5897|2. Source blocks new input and changes &lt;code>running|idle&lt;/code> to\n5898|   &lt;code>quiescing&lt;/code>.\n5899|3. Through &lt;code>handoff.quiesce&lt;/code>, source calls provider or task-board\n5900|   quiesce and waits for a complete safe boundary. A task-board source uses\n5901|   bridge &lt;code>export --mode handoff&lt;/code>, requires\n5902|   &lt;code>BridgeSafeBoundary.safe = true&lt;/code>, maps it exactly to RPC and\n5903|   checkpoint evidence, and retains its source-control token. Timeout or an\n5904|   incomplete bridge proof fails closed.\n5905|4. Source captures a fresh checkpoint under the current lease. A direct source\n5906|   uses the Section 7.5 Object Sink path for a portable provider snapshot or a\n5907|   validated zero-entry identity manifest for a backend-only provider; a\n5908|   task-board source uses only the opaque bundle. Both use the exact Section\n5909|   10.4 workspace-group root.\n5910|5. Source performs the final bulk record/blob/workspace/board sync to\n5911|   destination.\n5912|6. Destination stages, validates, and conflict-checks every referenced object.\n5913|   It does not resume.\n5914|7. Destination calls &lt;code>handoff.stop&lt;/code>. Source requests graceful\n5915|   provider/task-board stop, verifies process exit and durable-store closure,\n5916|   and records &lt;code>session.stopped&lt;/code>. A task-board source consumes the\n5917|   bridge source-control token with bridge &lt;code>stop&lt;/code>.\n5918|8. If normal exit appended provider/manager closure records, source captures a\n5919|   closure-only delta, creates a superseding validated checkpoint, and syncs\n5920|   that delta. Any unexpected workspace/background mutation fails the graceful\n5921|   flow while the source remains the stopped owner.\n5922|9. Destination calls tagged &lt;code>materialize.prepare&lt;/code> with\n5923|   &lt;code>intent = ownership_transfer&lt;/code>, the exact non-empty selected cohort\n5924|   in both cohort arrays, and kind workspace/provider/task-board/composite from\n5925|   the checkpoint sources. It then performs atomic materialization through RPC\n5926|   &lt;code>materialize.commit&lt;/code>, which leaves a durable rollbackable prepared\n5927|   transaction; a direct portable-store path invokes provider\n5928|   &lt;code>materialize&lt;/code> inside it. For task-board, destination also performs\n5929|   the journaled Section 10.6 import/open sequence inside commit, never before\n5930|   prepare. No prepared path accepts input.\n5931|10. After every migration-cohort member is stopped/prepared and group\n5932|   expectation still matches, destination creates each member's epoch\n5933|   &lt;code>source_epoch + 1&lt;/code>, predecessor source\n5934|   lease, reason &lt;code>graceful_takeover&lt;/code>, and checkpoint from step 4.\n5935|   When step 8 created a superseding checkpoint, that checkpoint replaces the\n5936|   step-4 checkpoint in this lease.\n5937|   Destination persists each lease, then calls &lt;code>handoff.commit&lt;/code> so source and\n5938|   destination union and persist that Lease Record. Destination MUST verify it\n5939|   is still the winning lease after union; if a concurrent higher/winning lease\n5940|   exists, it MUST NOT adopt or resume.\n5941|11. For a direct session, destination validates native discovery and resumes\n5942|    through &lt;code>ax pane SESSION_ID&lt;/code> with the checkpoint-derived\n5943|    effective profile and new fencing token, using plugin &lt;code>resume&lt;/code>.\n5944|    For task-board, destination performs no out-of-band adopt or resume.\n59\n… [40244 chars truncated for the reminder observer — judge f