or one-root provider/task-board, `validation_only` for backend-identity, full positive/negative objects and `validate_spec_contracts.py` 59 JSON/20 identities.\n- **Task-board subtransaction** as durable `TaskBoardJournalTransaction` with 4 stable bridge IDs, token/expiry/binding/cleanup invariants and common `prepare→import/open→commit→prepared→finalize` order (§10.6, §§13.3/13.6-13.10).\n- **Provider idempotency** sole key `(operation, operation_id)` (§7.5), other IDs immutable.\n- **Owner resume** as `prepare→commit→prepared→activation→finalize→committed` with 8 fixtures per kind (§13.10).\n- **Fork projection** `workspace_fork_v1` with bottom-up re-identification and language-neutral fixtures (§10.5, §13.8).\n- **Epoch-1 bootstrap** `creating` vs `failed/bootstrap_aborted` with null-checkpoint agreement across Event/RPC/CLI (§§13.1/13.2/13.9).\n- **Git submodule** isolated parent/child packs and triple-pointer rule (§§10.4/12.3, expected-red 128 cross-lookups).\n- **Profile authority** derived from checkpoint event-head closure (§§2.4/5.2/9.3/11.3/13).\n- **Digest path** `digest_path_v1 = sha256/HH/REST` and `MaterializationCohort` exact fields (§3.2, §11.3).\n\nDoD: settled-decision traceability (App. A.7), 23 versioned contracts, end-to-end lifecycle, honest provider/platform matrices (`portable_store=false`, Muse Windows unknown, Antigravity WSL2 conditional), conflict-safe replication/trust boundary/exclusions/CLI/errors/observability/rollout all normative; `validate_spec_contracts.py` (59/1/20/140/123/252) and `validate_second_rework.py` (116) pass, `task-board validate` pass, `git diff --check` 0, accepted evidence `0001f769…b569` cited, no product code discrepancy.\n\nArtifact: outcome resource `TASK-260819-1h306n_sixth-review-verdict.md` attached; board status `reviewing→done` set without `commit_ack` as required for reviewer-archetype. `STORY-260819-iscto1`/`EPIC-260819-1lxzng` reverted to `backlog` by board roll-up (other sibling tasks remain backlog);