qual\\nthe request tag (`SPEC.md:4373-4381`).\\n\\nThe commit-strategy rules are also incomplete. `atomic_directory_rename`\\nrequires a workspace directory operation, `atomic_file_merge` requires only\\nfile targets, and `two_phase_multi_root` requires at least two authorities or\\natomicity boundaries (`SPEC.md:3695-3700`). The normative provider operation is\\na provider-store `target_directory` (`SPEC.md:3627-3635`). Used alone in the\\nrequired `MAT-PROVIDER-ONLY` lane (`SPEC.md:4489`), it satisfies none of the\\nthree strategies. The same gap exists for a single task-board\\n`authority_root` installation. A mechanical truth-table check produced zero\\nlegal strategies for both one-root cases.\\n\\nDefine an exact kind/source/authority/action/validation/marker matrix and a\\nlegal strategy for every one-root provider and task-board transaction. Add\\ncomplete positive and negative Materialization Plan objects for all four kinds,\\nnot only tagged RPC wrappers.\\n\\n### 2. Task-board materialization has no durable subtransaction or crash-recovery contract\\n\\nBridge import/open/adopt produce and consume `import_token`, `open_token`,\\nstaged/dormant/manager references, expiry, and binding fac\n… [21960 chars truncated for the reminder observer — judge from the claim and evidence of a check, not the full body]</tool-result>\n  </message>\n  <message role=\"assistant\">\n    <reasoning-replay />\n  </message>\n  <message role=\"assistant\">\n    <tool-call call-id=\"c9\" name=\"read_file\"><arguments>{\"path\":\"SPEC.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":300}</arguments></tool-call>\n  </message>\n  <message role=\"tool\">\n    <tool-result call-id=\"c9\">Read text file `SPEC.md`.\n1|# Agent Session Manager (&lt;code>ax&lt;/code>) v0.1.0 Normative Specification\n2|\n3|| Field | Value |\n4|| --- | --- |\n5|| Specification release | &lt;code>v0.1.0&lt;/code> |\n6|| Document status | Review candidate and implementation contract |\n7|| Public command | &lt;code>ax&lt;/code> |\n8|| Repository | &lt;code>relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec&lt;/code> |\n9|| Default branch | &lt;code>main&lt;/code> |\n10|| License | MIT |\n11|| Author | Ivan Oparin &lt;code>&amp;lt;oparin@me.com&amp;gt;&lt;/code> |\n12|| Required release signature | SSH signing key &lt;code>~/.ssh/ivanopcode&lt;/code> |\n13|\n14|This document is the normative, implementation-ready contract for Agent Session\n15|Manager v0.1.0. It specifies behavior; it does not implement &lt;code>ax&lt;/code>.\n16|Provider facts explicitly marked conditional, unknown, or unsupported are\n17|version gates, not permission to invent parity.\n18|\n19|## 1. Conformance, language, and scope\n20|\n21|### 1.1 Normative language\n22|\n23|The key words MUST, MUST NOT, REQUIRED, SHALL, SHALL NOT, SHOULD, SHOULD NOT,\n24|RECOMMENDED, NOT RECOMMENDED, MAY, and OPTIONAL are to be interpreted as\n25|normative requirements when, and only when, they appear in uppercase.\n26|\n27|A conforming implementation MUST satisfy every MUST and MUST NOT applicable to\n28|its declared conformance targets. A deviation MAY exist only behind an\n29|experimental feature gate that is disabled by default, is reported by\n30|&lt;code>ax doctor&lt;/code>, and is never advertised as an available capability.\n31|\n32|### 1.2 Product boundary\n33|\n34|&lt;code>ax&lt;/code> manages durable coding-agent sessions across an explicitly\n35|trusted, allowlisted mesh of computers. It MUST let an operator:\n36|\n37|1. launch a direct provider session or a task-board-managed session;\n38|2. keep the terminal durable across a local terminal disconnect and, where the\n39|   terminal backend supports it, a reboot;\n40|3. list ownership and replica state across the mesh;\n41|4. synchronize immutable session metadata, provider state, task-board state,\n42|   and the workspace state required to resume;\n43|5. attach to the current owner without changing ownership;\n44|6. transfer ownership gracefully or, as an explicit recovery action, forcibly;\n45|7. fork from a checkpoint into a new logical session and workspace identity;\n46|8. stop a session without deleting its durable state; and\n47|9. resume a stopped session on its owner host.\n48|\n49|The v0.1.0 product is a Go CLI, optional per-user background service, provider\n50|plugin host, terminal supervisor, SSH RPC client/server, and Go-native\n51|replication engine. It is not:\n52|\n53|- a cloud service, public relay, or multi-tenant scheduler;\n54|- a replacement for a provider's native session store;\n55|- a replacement for task-board or &lt;code>tb-sessiond&lt;/code>;\n56|- a general-purpose backup, secrets manager, or source-control system;\n57|- a distributed shell that auto-authorizes discovered machines;\n58|- a guarantee that every provider supports every operation; or\n59|- an encrypted-at-rest snapshot product.\n60|\n61|There MUST be no permanent public TCP listener. The remote server entry point is\n62|&lt;code>ax rpc serve --stdio&lt;/code>, normally started by Tailscale SSH or ordinary\n63|OpenSSH.\n64|\n65|### 1.3 Conformance targets\n66|\n67|An implementation MUST declare one or more of these targets:\n68|\n69|| Target | Required behavior |\n70|| --- | --- |\n71|| Core CLI | Configuration, records, ownership, local list/status, direct provider lifecycle, structured errors |\n72|| Unix terminal backend | PTY management plus tmux integration on macOS, Linux, or WSL2 |\n73|| Windows terminal backend | Native PowerShell process supervision and ConPTY; no tmux claim |\n74|| Mesh peer | SSH stdio RPC, anti-entropy union sync, resumable blob transfer, staging, validation |\n75|| Workspace materializer | Conflict-safe Git and non-Git capture/materialization |\n76|| Provider adapter | Plugin protocol and only the capabilities advertised by probe |\n77|| Task-board bridge | Official\n… [16072 chars truncated for the reminder observer — judge from the claim and evidence of a check, not the full body]</tool-result>\n  </message>\n  <message role=\